On Sun, 21 Jan 2007, Randy Dunlap wrote:

> On Sun, 21 Jan 2007 02:36:55 -0500 (EST) Robert P. J. Day wrote:
>
> >
> >   just wondering.
>
> I have a few questions about it.
>
> Does the wiki replace the current TODO list? I dislike maintaining
> it in multiple places.

i wouldn't *replace* the current TODO list.  that list should be, as
the name suggests, stuff "to do."  however, once someone picks a
project, that should be entered into the wiki so others can keep track
of who's doing what, what progress they're making, issues they've run
into and so on.  and it should simultaneously be removed from the TODO
list.

quite simply, the current TODO list is too infrequently updated, and
anything that is currently being worked on shouldn't be in that list.

> Is it backed up so that once someone mucks it up, it can easily be
> fixed/restored?

i have no way to answer that.

